# Test 2 — nhom14 — [CLASSIFICATION THE RISK OF DIABETIC RETINOPATHY USING OCT IMAGES]

- Topic: Classification of diabetic retinopathy (DR) risk from OCT images — two branches: (A) Harvard-FairVision DR, (B) OLIVES
- Members (student ID) and roles:
  - 202414858 — M1, Branch A (FairVision-DR): GPU training, FIS, thresholds, latency. Responsible in this file for: B1, B2, B3 (FairVision part); A4
  - 202414864 — M2, Branch B (OLIVES): data, fold splitting, baselines, biomarkers. Responsible in this file for: B1, B2, B3 (OLIVES part); A3; B5
  - 202414861 — M3, Evaluation and data management: CIs, calibration, logistic baseline, FAIR, TRIPOD+AI, repository. Responsible in this file for: A1, C1–C4, B4, D
  - Each member reads 4 papers from A2 in full (assignment at the end of A2) and must be able to answer the key numbers of both branches.

## A. Literature review and research gaps

### A1. Search strategy

PubMed result counts were obtained by re-running the exact queries shown below on 09/11/2026 (PubMed, publication-year filter). The "Papers retained" column lists IDs from `DR_Literature_Review.xlsx`, assigned to the query matching each paper's topic.

| Source (PubMed, Scopus, IEEE Xplore, Google Scholar…) | Keywords / query | Years | Results | Papers retained |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| PubMed — Q1. DR epidemiology | `(diabetic retinopathy) AND (prevalence) AND (systematic review OR meta-analysis)` | 2020–2026 | 323 | 1 (#1) |
| PubMed — Q2. AI for DME detection on OCT | `(diabetic macular edema) AND (OCT) AND (deep learning OR artificial intelligence)` | 2020–2026 | 269 | 4 (#2, #6, #7, #8) |
| PubMed — Q3. Predicting anti-VEGF response | `(diabetic macular edema) AND (anti-VEGF) AND (OCT) AND (deep learning OR predict*)` | 2020–2026 | 131 | 5 (#9, #10, #12, #13, #14) |
| PubMed — Q4. AI on OCTA for DR | `(diabetic retinopathy) AND (OCTA OR OCT angiography) AND (deep learning OR machine learning)` | 2020–2026 | 112 | 10 (#3, #4, #15–#22) |
| PubMed — Q5. DR screening on fundus photographs, real-world validation | `(diabetic retinopathy) AND (fundus photograph*) AND (deep learning) AND (validation OR screening)` | 2020–2026 | 183 | 6 (#5, #24–#28) |
| PubMed — Q6. Retinal foundation models | `(foundation model) AND (retinal OR retina) AND (self-supervised)` | 2020–2026 | 33 | 1 (#29) |
| PubMed — Q7. Public OCT/OCTA datasets and benchmarks | `(retinal OCT OR OCTA) AND (public dataset OR benchmark) AND (diabetic OR macular edema)` | 2014–2026 (extended to capture original dataset papers) | 78 | 9 (#30, #31, #34–#40) |
| arXiv, Google Scholar (by dataset name); backward citation from the papers above | `FairVision`, `Harvard-FairVision30k`, `OLIVES dataset`; reference lists of #2, #3, #4 | No limit | Not applicable — searched by name or citation, no result count | 4 (#11, #23, #32, #33) |
| **Total** | | | **1,129 hits** across the 7 PubMed queries (not de-duplicated across queries) | **40 papers**: 35 from 2020–2026, 5 from 2014–2019 |

Characteristics of the 40 retained papers: 34 Q1, 3 Q2, 2 conference papers (NeurIPS D&B, ICAART), 1 preprint (arXiv); 5 reviews or meta-analyses (#1–#5), 11 original dataset/benchmark papers (#30–#40), 24 model development, validation or method-comparison studies (#6–#29).

Inclusion / exclusion criteria:
- Include: (1) AI/ML on OCT or OCTA for DR/DME: detection, grading, prediction of treatment response; (2) papers using fundus photographs but with OCT-derived labels (#7, #8), or providing evidence on external validation and real-world deployment (#24–#28), used for gaps G1 and G2; (3) reviews, meta-analyses and epidemiology as background; (4) original papers of public datasets the team uses or could use; (5) preference for Q1/Q2 journals published 2020–2026.
- Exclude: papers without quantitative results; fundus-only papers with no OCT labels, no external validation and no real-world deployment; papers not on DR/DME (e.g., AMD or glaucoma only), except original dataset papers; papers without a traceable DOI or link; duplicates (latest full version kept).
- Justified exceptions: 5 pre-2020 papers (#34, #35, #38, #39, #40) kept as original papers of public datasets; the FairVision preprint (#33) and the NeurIPS OLIVES paper (#32) because they are the sources of the two datasets the team uses; the ICAART conference paper (#11) as one of the few studies using a Siamese network to predict anti-VEGF response.
- Acknowledged weaknesses: (1) the search history was not saved when the matrix was built, so the counts above are **re-run** counts from 09/11/2026; the number of papers excluded at each screening stage (title, abstract, full text) is not available and is not reported; (2) papers were assigned to queries by topic, and some may have been found through citations rather than in the query results.

